WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.468
Video eighteen. GSTR-1 and GSTR-3B.

00:00:05.668 --> 00:00:09.019
You enter the sales invoices and the purchase
bills.

00:00:08.949 --> 00:00:13.434
GSTR-1 collects the outward supplies, table by
table.

00:00:13.364 --> 00:00:18.916
GSTR-3B adds the input tax of the purchases,
and shows the tax to pay.

00:00:18.846 --> 00:00:22.197
Each return goes to the portal as a JSON file.

00:00:22.497 --> 00:00:27.780
Press Alt+G, and type GSTR-1. The report opens
on the current month.

00:00:28.478 --> 00:00:35.428
Alt+F2 changes the period: April to October. 17
vouchers: 5 are in the return, 1 is uncertain.

00:00:36.128 --> 00:00:42.878
The Return View shows each table. Enter on B2B shows the
three invoices, with the GSTIN of each buyer.

00:00:43.358 --> 00:00:49.309
17 vouchers in the period. 5 go into the
return. The others are not relevant for GST.

00:00:49.239 --> 00:00:52.922
One voucher is uncertain. Correct it before
you file.

00:00:53.222 --> 00:00:57.679
Uncertain Transactions lists each voucher with
its reason. Joshi Stores

00:00:57.329 --> 00:01:00.705
is a registered dealer, but the ledger has no
GSTIN.

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:07.142
Alt+E exports the return. Hisaab asks: 1 uncertain
voucher is not in the return. Export?

00:01:07.172 --> 00:01:12.123
Y writes the JSON file. Upload it on the GST
portal with the offline tool.

00:01:13.392 --> 00:01:20.078
GSTR-3B uses the same vouchers. Table 3.1
shows the outward supplies and their tax.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:28.250
Table 4 shows the input tax credit of the
purchases: ₹13,875 of IGST.

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:32.081
Next video: e-Invoice and e-Way Bill.

